This version correctly addresses the majority of the grammatical issues present in the original paragraph. It properly uses the present tense ("doesn't remember"), corrects "I thinks" to "I think," and "he are" to "he's." It also changes "she's say" to "she said" for correct verb tense and "I responds" to "I responded" for subject-verb agreement. Furthermore, it replaces "ain't no sure" with "I'm not sure," which is a more grammatically correct and polite way to express uncertainty. Lastly, "Did you found it?" is corrected to "Did you find it?" which is the proper way to form the question in the past tense.

